---
import ToolLayout from '../../components/ToolLayout.astro';
import Toggle from '../../components/Toggle.astro';
import { COMMANDS, EXAMPLE_LOG } from '../../lib/at-decoder';
import { toolUrl } from '../../utils/paths';

const references = [
  {
    title: '3GPP TS 27.007 — AT command set for User Equipment (UE)',
    href: 'https://portal.3gpp.org/desktopmodules/Specifications/SpecificationDetails.aspx?specificationId=1515',
    note: 'all parameter values and the +CME ERROR tables (§9.2). Checked against V20.0.0.',
  },
  {
    title: '3GPP TS 24.301 — Non-Access-Stratum (NAS) protocol for EPS; Stage 3',
    href: 'https://portal.3gpp.org/desktopmodules/Specifications/SpecificationDetails.aspx?specificationId=1072',
    note: 'Table 9.9.3.9.1, EMM cause values used by +CEREG <reject_cause>. Checked against V20.1.0.',
  },
  {
    title: '3GPP TS 24.008 — Mobile radio interface Layer 3 specification; Core network protocols',
    href: 'https://portal.3gpp.org/desktopmodules/Specifications/SpecificationDetails.aspx?specificationId=1015',
    note: 'GPRS Timer 2 / 3 (T3324, T3412) and Extended DRX parameters coding.',
  },
  {
    title: '3GPP TS 23.003 — Numbering, addressing and identification',
    href: 'https://portal.3gpp.org/desktopmodules/Specifications/SpecificationDetails.aspx?specificationId=729',
    note: 'IMSI and IMEI structure, IMEI check digit (Annex B).',
  },
  { title: 'ITU-T V.250 — Serial asynchronous automatic dialling and control', note: 'OK, ERROR and other final result codes' },
];

const supported = Object.keys(COMMANDS)
  .filter((c) => c !== 'CME')
  .map((c) => `+${c}`);
---

<ToolLayout slug="at-decoder" references={references}>
  <form id="at-form" novalidate>
    <div class="tool-grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2 class="panel-title">Modem log</h2>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="f-log">Paste AT commands, responses and URCs</label>
          <textarea id="f-log" name="log" rows="16" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" class="mono" data-no-url aria-describedby="f-log-help">{EXAMPLE_LOG}</textarea>
          <p class="help" id="f-log-help">
            Timestamps and <code>&lt;&lt;</code> / <code>&gt;&gt;</code> markers are ignored. Your log stays in your browser
            and is never put in the page URL, since it may contain your IMEI and IMSI.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: var(--s3)">
          <button type="button" class="btn" id="load-example">Load example</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn" id="clear-log">Clear</button>
        </div>
        <div class="fields fields--wide" style="margin-top: var(--s4)">
          <Toggle name="quiet" label="Hide OK and plain text lines" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="at-sum">
        <h2 class="panel-title" id="at-sum">Modem state at the end of the log</h2>
        <dl class="results" id="summary"></dl>
        <p class="help" id="summary-empty" hidden>Nothing decoded yet. Paste lines such as <code>+CEREG: 1,"1A2D","01A2D101",7</code>.</p>
        <p class="help" id="counts" style="margin-top: var(--s3)"></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </form>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="at-lines">
    <h2 id="at-lines">Line by line</h2>
    <div id="lines" class="lines" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="formula">
    <p>
      Every line is classified first. Lines starting with <code>AT</code> are commands sent by the host. <code>OK</code>,
      <code>ERROR</code> and <code>+CME ERROR</code> end a command. A <code>+XXX:</code> line is a response when it
      follows <code>AT+XXX?</code> or an execute command of the same name before the final result code. Otherwise it is an
      unsolicited result code (URC).
    </p>
    <p>
      Without the command line, the form is guessed from the parameters. <code>+CEREG: 2,1</code> is a read response
      (<code>&lt;n&gt;,&lt;stat&gt;</code>) because a URC's second field would be a quoted tracking area code.
      <code>+CSCON: 0,1</code> stays ambiguous and is flagged. Paste the command lines too for an exact decode.
    </p>
    <p>
      Measurement indices map to ranges, not single values: <code>&lt;rsrp&gt;</code> = n means −141 + n ≤ RSRP &lt; −140 + n
      dBm, and <code>&lt;rsrq&gt;</code> = n means −20 + n/2 ≤ RSRQ &lt; −19.5 + n/2 dB. The E-UTRAN cell ID is 28 bits, and its
      upper 20 bits are the eNB ID for a macro eNB. The IMEI check digit uses the Luhn algorithm.
    </p>
    <p>Decoded commands: {supported.join(', ')}, plus <code>+CME ERROR</code> and the V.250 final result codes.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>Reading a cellular modem log</h2>
    <p>
      LTE-M and NB-IoT modules from every vendor share the AT commands of 3GPP TS 27.007. The answers are dense:
      <code>+CEREG: 1,"1A2D","01A2D101",7,,,"00000110","00101000"</code> says the module is registered on its home
      network, gives the tracking area and cell, and reports the PSM timers the network granted. Decoding that by hand
      means juggling four specifications. This page does it line by line and keeps a running summary of the modem state.
    </p>
    <h3>Registration first</h3>
    <p>
      <code>&lt;stat&gt;</code> in <code>+CEREG</code> is the first thing to check. 2 means still searching, 3 means
      the network rejected the module, and 1 or 5 means registered. Use <code>AT+CEREG=5</code> during bring-up: the
      URCs then also carry the EMM reject cause and the PSM timers. Cause #15, "no suitable cells in tracking area", is
      common when the SIM is not provisioned for LTE-M or NB-IoT on that network. Cause #11 and #14 point to the
      subscription or roaming agreement.
    </p>
    <h3>Signal: use +CESQ, not +CSQ</h3>
    <p>
      <code>+CSQ</code> dates from GSM and modules derive it from LTE measurements in their own way. <code>+CESQ</code>
      reports RSRP and RSRQ, the values the network uses. The fields for other RATs read 99 or 255 ("not known or not
      detectable"). Signal alone does not tell you the coverage level: LTE-M and NB-IoT work far below normal LTE
      levels by repeating transmissions, at the cost of power. The <a href={toolUrl('lte-power')}>LTE-M power budget</a>
      shows what repetitions do to battery life.
    </p>
    <h3>What the network granted</h3>
    <p>
      <code>AT+CPSMS</code> and <code>AT+CEDRXS</code> only request power-saving timers. The network decides, and the
      granted values arrive in <code>+CEREG</code> (n=4 or 5), <code>+CEDRXP</code> and <code>+CEDRXRDP</code>. They
      often differ from the request, sometimes a lot. Use the <a href={toolUrl('psm-edrx')}>PSM &amp; eDRX calculator</a> to
      encode new requests.
    </p>
    <h3>Errors</h3>
    <p>
      Turn on <code>AT+CMEE=1</code> (numeric) or <code>AT+CMEE=2</code> (text) early in your init sequence: a bare
      <code>ERROR</code> tells you nothing. Codes 0–100 are general errors. Codes above 100 map to network causes, with the
      TS 24.301 cause number shown as <code>(#n)</code>. Codes from 256 up are manufacturer-specific.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>

<script>
  import { bindForm, esc } from '../../scripts/tool-client';
  import { decodeLog, EXAMPLE_LOG, summarize, type Decoded, type LineKind } from '../../lib/at-decoder';
  import type { Values } from '../../lib/url-state';

  const KIND: Record<LineKind, string> = {
    command: 'Sent',
    response: 'Response',
    urc: 'URC',
    final: 'Result',
    error: 'Error',
    info: 'Text',
    unknown: 'Not decoded',
  };

  const form = document.getElementById('at-form') as HTMLFormElement;
  const log = form.elements.namedItem('log') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
  const linesEl = document.getElementById('lines')!;
  const summaryEl = document.getElementById('summary')!;
  const countsEl = document.getElementById('counts')!;

  const toneClass = (t?: string) => (t === 'bad' ? 'error' : t ?? '');

  function card(d: Decoded): string {
    const fields = d.fields.length
      ? `<table class="atl-fields"><tbody>${d.fields
          .map(
            (f) =>
              `<tr class="${f.tone ? `t-${toneClass(f.tone)}` : ''}"><th scope="row" class="mono">${esc(f.name)}</th><td class="mono">${esc(f.value)}</td><td>${esc(f.meaning)}</td></tr>`,
          )
          .join('')}</tbody></table>`
      : '';
    const notes = d.notes.length ? `<ul class="atl-notes">${d.notes.map((n) => `<li>${esc(n)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>` : '';
    const compact = !d.fields.length && (d.kind === 'final' || d.kind === 'info');
    return `<article class="atl atl--${d.kind}${d.tone ? ` atl--${toneClass(d.tone)}` : ''}${compact ? ' atl--compact' : ''}">
      <div class="atl-head"><code class="atl-raw">${esc(d.raw.trim())}</code><span class="atl-kind">${KIND[d.kind]}</span></div>
      ${compact ? (d.notes[0] ? `<p class="atl-title">${esc(d.notes[0])}</p>` : '') : `<p class="atl-title">${esc(d.title)}${d.ref ? ` <span class="atl-ref">${esc(d.ref)}</span>` : ''}</p>${fields}${notes}`}
    </article>`;
  }

  function update(v: Values) {
    const decoded = decodeLog(v.log ?? '');
    const quiet = v.quiet === '1';
    const shown = quiet ? decoded.filter((d) => !(d.kind === 'info' || (d.kind === 'final' && d.tone === 'ok'))) : decoded;
    linesEl.innerHTML = shown.length ? shown.map(card).join('') : '<p class="help">No lines to show.</p>';

    const sum = summarize(decoded);
    summaryEl.innerHTML = sum
      .map(
        (s) =>
          `<div class="result"><dt>${esc(s.label)}</dt><dd><span class="sum-val${s.tone ? ` t-${toneClass(s.tone)}` : ''}">${esc(s.value)}</span></dd></div>`,
      )
      .join('');
    document.getElementById('summary-empty')!.hidden = sum.length > 0;

    const n = (k: LineKind) => decoded.filter((d) => d.kind === k).length;
    const parts = [
      `${decoded.length} line${decoded.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,
      `${n('command')} command${n('command') === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,
      `${n('response')} response${n('response') === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,
      `${n('urc')} URC${n('urc') === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,
      `${n('error') + decoded.filter((d) => d.kind === 'final' && d.tone === 'bad').length} error(s)`,
    ];
    if (n('unknown')) parts.push(`${n('unknown')} not decoded`);
    countsEl.textContent = decoded.length ? parts.join(' · ') : '';
  }

  const rerun = bindForm(form, update);
  document.getElementById('load-example')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
    log.value = EXAMPLE_LOG;
    rerun();
  });
  document.getElementById('clear-log')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
    log.value = '';
    rerun();
    log.focus();
  });
</script>

<style>
  p code {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  textarea.mono {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .lines {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s2);
  }
  :global(.atl) {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--s2) var(--s3);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  :global(.atl--command) {
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  :global(.atl--ok) {
    border-left-color: var(--ok);
  }
  :global(.atl--warn) {
    border-left-color: var(--warn);
  }
  :global(.atl--error) {
    border-left-color: var(--error);
  }
  :global(.atl--compact) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--s3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding-block: var(--s1);
  }
  :global(.atl--compact .atl-head) {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
  }
  :global(.atl--compact .atl-title) {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  :global(.atl-head) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--s3);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  :global(.atl-raw) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  :global(.atl-kind) {
    flex: none;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  :global(.atl-title) {
    margin: var(--s1) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  :global(.atl-ref) {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-left: var(--s1);
  }
  :global(.atl-fields) {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: var(--s2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  :global(.atl-fields th),
  :global(.atl-fields td) {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 0.2rem var(--s3) 0.2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  :global(.atl-fields th) {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
    width: 1%;
  }
  :global(.atl-fields td.mono) {
    width: 1%;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.atl-fields tr.t-ok td:last-child) {
    color: var(--ok);
  }
  :global(.atl-fields tr.t-warn td:last-child) {
    color: var(--warn);
  }
  :global(.atl-fields tr.t-error td:last-child) {
    color: var(--error);
  }
  :global(.atl-notes) {
    margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  :global(.sum-val) {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-align: right;
  }
  :global(.sum-val.t-ok) {
    color: var(--ok);
  }
  :global(.sum-val.t-warn) {
    color: var(--warn);
  }
  :global(.sum-val.t-error) {
    color: var(--error);
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    :global(.sum-val) {
      text-align: left;
    }
    :global(.atl-fields tr) {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
      column-gap: var(--s3);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      padding: 0.2rem 0;
    }
    :global(.atl-fields th),
    :global(.atl-fields td) {
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      width: auto;
    }
    :global(.atl-fields td:last-child) {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
